# A FIXTURE FOR THE PACK, and it is a fixture precisely because it is boring.
#
# playtest_bridge is where zombies get PLAYED; this is where they get measured.
# CLAUDE.md's rule is that a long sweep runs on a fixture with nothing else moving
# in it -- a probe that shares a map with live shooters and rushers reads every
# stray ball as "the zombie did that", and two rounds of this project's history
# were spent on exactly that mistake.
#
# So: flat deck, no holes, no pillars, no other hazard of any kind, and THREE
# graves spaced far enough apart that no single visit is inside two trigger radii
# (ZOMBIE_TRIGGER_RADIUS is 9 m; the cells are 2 m, so ten cells apart is comfortably
# clear). Three rather than one because a grave is spent once and several phases
# need a fresh one.
#
# Every cell around each grave is deck, which is the rule the validator enforces
# and the dressing pass respects: a pack of five spawns on a ring that spills into
# the neighbouring cells, and a member over a hole falls the instant it exists.

name = test_zombies
base_height = 0
width = 20
length = 24
tags = foot, test, zombie

